msgstr "Do not communicate on this channel."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2221
msgctxt "drone-incCall"
msgid ""
"DISENGAGE!\n"
"\n"
"Captain, it's not what it looks like. Please dock with us and we will "
"explain everything."
msgstr "DISENGAGE!\n\nCaptain, it's not what it looks like. Please dock with us and we will explain everything."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2245
msgctxt "wormhole-incCall"
msgid ""
"RED ALERT!\n"
"\n"
"Captain, a bomb has just gone off on our station and we are under attack "
"from the Kraylor. We need your help immediately!"
msgstr "RED ALERT!\n\nCaptain, a bomb has just gone off on our station and we are under attack from the Kraylor. We need your help immediately!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2251
msgctxt "wormhole-shipLog"
msgid "Defend the Wormhole Station"
msgstr "Defend the Wormhole Station"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2302
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid ""
"Hello Captain. Have you noticed our cool wormhole?\n"
"\n"
"We're studying the energy radiating from the wormhole, and the similarities "
"to black holes are astonishing. Please drop by if you'd like to help out."
msgstr "Hello Captain. Have you noticed our cool wormhole?\n\nWe're studying the energy radiating from the wormhole, and the similarities to black holes are astonishing. Please drop by if you'd like to help out."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2313
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Please bring us the spare parts!"
msgstr "Please bring us the spare parts!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2317
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Thanks so much for your help!"
msgstr "Thanks so much for your help!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2328
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid ""
"Thanks for dropping by, Captain.\n"
"\n"
"Our research is going well, but we could use some spare stabilizers for our "
"Hawking Scanner. Would you mind salvaging some for us from the other side of "
"the wormhole?"
msgstr "Thanks for dropping by, Captain.\n\nOur research is going well, but we could use some spare stabilizers for our Hawking Scanner. Would you mind salvaging some for us from the other side of the wormhole?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2334
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Okay, we can help with that."
msgstr "Okay, we can help with that."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2337
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Do you pay tips?"
msgstr "Do you pay tips?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2339
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Maybe later, then. Goodbye."
msgstr "Maybe later, then. Goodbye."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2354
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid ""
"Thanks for your help, Captain!\n"
"\n"
"These spare parts will really help with the program budget."
msgstr "Thanks for your help, Captain!\n\nThese spare parts will really help with the program budget."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2362
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "What do we get for being your errand boy?"
msgstr "What do we get for being your errand boy?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2368
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "You get half of what would have with a smarter attitude! So rude."
msgstr "You get half of what would have with a smarter attitude! So rude."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2377
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "We're so glad we could help"
msgstr "We're so glad we could help"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2380
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "We are too. Thanks a bunch."
msgstr "We are too. Thanks a bunch."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2390
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid ""
"We still need those spare parts from X472 on the other side of the wormhole!"
msgstr "We still need those spare parts from X472 on the other side of the wormhole!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2395
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Thanks that was awesome"
msgstr "Thanks that was awesome"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2404
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "We're under attack. Help us!"
msgstr "We're under attack. Help us!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2413
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Come pick up our Hawking Scanner for repairs."
msgstr "Come pick up our Hawking Scanner for repairs."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2423
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Please find someone to repair our Hawking Scanner."
msgstr "Please find someone to repair our Hawking Scanner."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2437
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid ""
"Thanks again, Captain.\n"
"\n"
"We need you to find someone to repair this Hawking Scanner. Please bring it "
"back once it's working again."
msgstr "Thanks again, Captain.\n\nWe need you to find someone to repair this Hawking Scanner. Please bring it back once it's working again."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2443
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Any idea where we should take it?"
msgstr "Any idea where we should take it?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2448
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid ""
"One of the nebula researchers should be able to point you in the right "
"direction.\n"
"\n"
"If you're not sure where to find them, ask for directions at the Admin "
"Station"
msgstr "One of the nebula researchers should be able to point you in the right direction.\n\nIf you're not sure where to find them, ask for directions at the Admin Station"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2458
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Have you considered shoving it where the sun don't shine?"
msgstr "Have you considered shoving it where the sun don't shine?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2462
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "What is it with you, anyways?"
msgstr "What is it with you, anyways?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2472
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid ""
"You got it fixed?\n"
"\n"
"That's amazing, Captain. Thank you so much! You and your crew are true heros "
"of our system; may your names live on through history.\n"
"\n"
"Glory to you and your kin."
msgstr "You got it fixed?\n\nThat's amazing, Captain. Thank you so much! You and your crew are true heros of our system; may your names live on through history.\n\nGlory to you and your kin."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2479
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "You're very welcome."
msgstr "You're very welcome."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2484
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Goodbye captain. May peace be with you."
msgstr "Goodbye captain. May peace be with you."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2490
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "Kiss my feet!"
msgstr "Kiss my feet!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2497
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid ""
"I was about to call this in to Admin and have them declare you victorious, "
"but I've had enough of you.\n"
"\n"
"YOU MAY BE A HERO, BUT YOU'RE ALSO A JERK!"
msgstr "I was about to call this in to Admin and have them declare you victorious, but I've had enough of you.\n\nYOU MAY BE A HERO, BUT YOU'RE ALSO A JERK!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2504
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "A real peach, you are."
msgstr "A real peach, you are."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2514
msgctxt "colony-comms"
msgid "Well, what I can do for you?"
msgstr "Well, what I can do for you?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2521
msgctxt "colony-comms"
msgid "We're looking for Dr. Hendrix"
msgstr "We're looking for Dr. Hendrix"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2531
msgctxt "colony-comms"
msgid ""
"I.....zzzZ\n"
"Hello?\n"
"...\n"
"The nearby NeZula somzzzzzzimes messssssses with our long range "
"commcommcommcomm somet...\n"
"\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"....dock...pr...b..\n"
"...r"
msgstr "I.....zzzZ\nHello?\n...\nThe nearby NeZula somzzzzzzimes messssssses with our long range commcommcommcomm somet...\n\n...\n\n....dock...pr...b..\n...r"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2544
msgctxt "colony-comms"
msgid ""
"I am Dr. Hendrix.\n"
"\n"
"If I remember that voice correctly, you are the crew from the Navy ship that "
"saved me when I was stranded in the nebula!\n"
"\n"
"What can I do for you?"
msgstr "I am Dr. Hendrix.\n\nIf I remember that voice correctly, you are the crew from the Navy ship that saved me when I was stranded in the nebula!\n\nWhat can I do for you?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2553
msgctxt "colony-comms"
msgid "Can you fix this Hawking Scanner?"
msgstr "Can you fix this Hawking Scanner?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2559
msgctxt "colony-comms"
msgid ""
"Let me have a look...\n"
"\n"
"Ah, I see why it's giving you trouble. Everything reads as okay, but the "
"Graviton Lens is mis-calibrated somehow so it's throwing off the whole "
"system.\n"
"\n"
"The good news is that it's easy to swap these out, the tech at the wormhole "
"station should be able to do it. The bad news is that we have a shortage of "
"Graviton Lenses right now because of those drone convoys.\n"
"\n"
"I've put in a requisition for one in your name. If you can find one in a "
"Navy storehouse, bring it to the wormhole station and they should be good to "
"go."
msgstr "Let me have a look...\n\nAh, I see why it's giving you trouble. Everything reads as okay, but the Graviton Lens is mis-calibrated somehow so it's throwing off the whole system.\n\nThe good news is that it's easy to swap these out, the tech at the wormhole station should be able to do it. The bad news is that we have a shortage of Graviton Lenses right now because of those drone convoys.\n\nI've put in a requisition for one in your name. If you can find one in a Navy storehouse, bring it to the wormhole station and they should be good to go."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2569
msgctxt "colony-shipLog"
msgid "Find a Graviton Lens"
msgstr "Find a Graviton Lens"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2584
msgctxt "colony-comms"
msgid "Some filler text and whatever. What are we even doing here?"
msgstr "Some filler text and whatever. What are we even doing here?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2587
msgctxt "colony-comms"
msgid "Dude, where even ARE we?"
msgstr "Dude, where even ARE we?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2597
msgctxt "checkpointsStn-comms"
msgid "Not much here bud, just doing checkpoint kinda things, ya know?"
msgstr "Not much here bud, just doing checkpoint kinda things, ya know?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2606
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid "Defend the SW Checkpoint now!"
msgstr "Defend the SW Checkpoint now!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2613
#, lua-format
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid ""
"You are on 'patrol'.\n"
"See that you make it to %s next."
msgstr "You are on 'patrol'.\nSee that you make it to %s next."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2626
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid "Your orders are to follow the convoy to see where it goes"
msgstr "Your orders are to follow the convoy to see where it goes"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2634
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid "Your orders are to join a convoy and infiltrate the drone nests."
msgstr "Your orders are to join a convoy and infiltrate the drone nests."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2642
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid ""
"Your orders are to scan those beacons and find the defense grid controller"
msgstr "Your orders are to scan those beacons and find the defence grid controller"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2655
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid ""
"We are keeping the 007, and you can continue to fly it, or switch back to "
"the Propitious 1 at any time. We'll keep it docked here at the station for "
"you."
msgstr "We are keeping the 007, and you can continue to fly it, or switch back to the Propitious 1 at any time. We'll keep it docked here at the station for you."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2662
#, lua-format
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid ""
"Great work, Captain!\n"
"Destroying the central control eliminated all the other drone stations and "
"stopped the convoys in their tracks! Of course, you are authorized to mop up "
"any resistance that might remain, but we're calling this a job well done.\n"
"%s"
msgstr "Great work, Captain!\nDestroying the central control eliminated all the other drone stations and stopped the convoys in their tracks! Of course, you are authorised to mop up any resistance that might remain, but we're calling this a job well done.\n%s"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2675
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid ""
"Good day, soldier.\n"
"\n"
"We shouldn't talk over this channel, please dock to the station when you "
"have a chance."
msgstr "Good day, soldier.\n\nWe shouldn't talk over this channel, please dock to the station when you have a chance."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2686
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid ""
"Welcome aboard.\n"
"\n"
"We need you to patrol the area. It's not exciting work, but it's got to be "
"done. No rush, just make sure you visit each checkpoint in order, and we'll "
"let you know if anything more pressing comes up."
msgstr "Welcome aboard.\n\nWe need you to patrol the area. It's not exciting work, but it's got to be done. No rush, just make sure you visit each checkpoint in order, and we'll let you know if anything more pressing comes up."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2692
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid "Okay. We're ready to start the patrol"
msgstr "Okay. We're ready to start the patrol"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2701
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid ""
"Welcome back, Captain.\n"
"\n"
"We've tracked that convoy to a huge nest of drone stations in the west. The "
"stations all form part of one proximity defense grid, and we have identified "
"some beacons that appear to be related to its operation. We're hoping that "
"if we can get a closer look at them, we might be able to figure out how to "
"knock out the central control.\n"
"\n"
"There is a drone ship docked here which you can use to infiltrate the nests. "
"If you arrive with a convoy, you should automatically be granted access and "
"we think the proximity defenses will remain disabled while you stay in the "
"area. Of course, if you start firing, then all bets are probably off.\n"
"\n"
"Hop in that drone ship, find the beacons, and get close enough to scan them "
"- EASY!"
msgstr "Welcome back, Captain.\n\nWe've tracked that convoy to a huge nest of drone stations in the west. The stations all form part of one proximity defence grid, and we have identified some beacons that appear to be related to its operation. We're hoping that if we can get a closer look at them, we might be able to figure out how to knock out the central control.\n\nThere is a drone ship docked here which you can use to infiltrate the nests. If you arrive with a convoy, you should automatically be granted access and we think the proximity defences will remain disabled while you stay in the area. Of course, if you start firing, then all bets are probably off.\n\nHop in that drone ship, find the beacons, and get close enough to scan them - EASY!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2713
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid "We're ready to infiltrate the drone nest"
msgstr "We're ready to infiltrate the drone nest"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2720
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid "(Object) Isn't that a treaty violation!?"
msgstr "(Object) Isn't that a treaty violation!?"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:2726
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid ""
"(Objecting)\n"
"Sir, decoding the communications of alien defense systems is a violation of "
"the Deepspace Militarized Citizenry Accord (DMCA).\n"
"[...]\n"
"Captain, are you angling for a good samaritan's award or something? Get out "
"of here with that legal mumbo-jumbo.\n"
"\n"
"However you want to do it, you need to find that central control. Get on it!"
