#, lua-format
msgctxt "attack-incCall"
msgid ""
"HELP!\n"
"We are taking damage from %s and might need assistance."
msgstr "HELP!\nWe are taking damage from %s and might need assistance."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3263
#, lua-format
msgctxt "attack-shipLog"
msgid "%s is taking damage!"
msgstr "%s is taking damage!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3296
msgctxt "adminStn-comms"
msgid ""
"Sorry to interrupt, but we've just recieved an urgent call.\n"
"\n"
"It seems one of our researchers, Dr. Hendrix, and her crew have lost their "
"way in a nearby nebula and need our help. They were running experiments in "
"the nebula when their engines and transponder went offline. Please follow "
"our scout vessel, SR7, to the nebula and search for them."
msgstr "Sorry to interrupt, but we've just recieved an urgent call.\n\nIt seems one of our researchers, Dr. Hendrix, and her crew have lost their way in a nearby nebula and need our help. They were running experiments in the nebula when their engines and transponder went offline. Please follow our scout vessel, SR7, to the nebula and search for them."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3321
msgctxt "adminStn-comms"
msgid "Meet me at the edge of the nebula"
msgstr "Meet me at the edge of the nebula"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3359
msgctxt "adminStn-incCall"
msgid ""
"Ready to head in?\n"
"\n"
"The nebula is very thick, so we will need to get close to find a ship with "
"no transponder. Probes won't show the ship, but your relay station should be "
"able to pick it up at 20U or less. There may be hazards, so be careful.\n"
"\n"
"I'll follow you. Let's find Dr. Hendrix and bring her crew home."
msgstr "Ready to head in?\n\nThe nebula is very thick, so we will need to get close to find a ship with no transponder. Probes won't show the ship, but your relay station should be able to pick it up at 20U or less. There may be hazards, so be careful.\n\nI'll follow you. Let's find Dr. Hendrix and bring her crew home."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3367
msgctxt "adminStn-shipLog"
msgid "Fly into the Nebula and find Dr. Hendrix"
msgstr "Fly into the Nebula and find Dr. Hendrix"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3412
msgctxt "finishMissionNebulae-shipLog"
msgid "Sensors have been upgraded."
msgstr "Sensors have been upgraded."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3462
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid ""
"Great!\n"
"\n"
"Start at the checkpoint in the North West. You'll need to dock at each "
"station before proceeding to the next."
msgstr "Great!\n\nStart at the checkpoint in the North West. You'll need to dock at each station before proceeding to the next."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3508
#, lua-format
msgctxt "defenceStn-incCall"
msgid "Please proceed to %s"
msgstr "Please proceed to %s"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3514
#, lua-format
msgctxt "defenceStn-shipLog"
msgid "Please proceed to %s"
msgstr "Please proceed to %s"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3541
msgctxt "defenceStn-incCall"
msgid ""
"Great work captain!\n"
"\n"
"You have repelled the attackers and the SW Checkpoint is safe for now, but "
"intelligence reports show a huge drone convoy in your vicinity to the NW.\n"
"\n"
"INVESTIGATE BUT DO NOT ENGAGE! We have it on good word that attacking this "
"convoy is extremely risky. Keep your distance, but we'd like to know where "
"they are going."
msgstr "Great work captain!\n\nYou have repelled the attackers and the SW Checkpoint is safe for now, but intelligence reports show a huge drone convoy in your vicinity to the NW.\n\nINVESTIGATE BUT DO NOT ENGAGE! We have it on good word that attacking this convoy is extremely risky. Keep your distance, but we'd like to know where they are going."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3551
msgctxt "defenceStn-shipLog"
msgid "Investigate the convoy, but DO NOT ENGAGE"
msgstr "Investigate the convoy, but DO NOT ENGAGE"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3596
msgctxt "defenceStn-incCall"
msgid ""
"Come in, Captain.\n"
"We have the info we need about that convoy and strongly discourage any "
"further engagement.\n"
"Your assistance is required with a secret mission. Dock with us to receive "
"further instructions when you're ready."
msgstr "Come in, Captain.\nWe have the info we need about that convoy and strongly discourage any further engagement.\nYour assistance is required with a secret mission. Dock with us to receive further instructions when you're ready."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3602
msgctxt "defenceStn-shipLog"
msgid "Dock with the Defence Station to start another mission"
msgstr "Dock with the Defence Station to start another mission"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3651
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "and when in doubt - apply missiles."
msgstr "and when in doubt - apply missiles."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3655
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "and we've given you some extra missiles to help get the job done."
msgstr "and we've given you some extra missiles to help get the job done."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3664
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid "and go find some extra missiles to help get the job done."
msgstr "and go find some extra missiles to help get the job done."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3672
#, lua-format
msgctxt "wormhole-comms"
msgid ""
"Great!\n"
"There is an old Exuari station, callsign X472, to the SE on the other side "
"of the wormhole. It used to study the planet forming nearby, but it's been "
"abandoned for over a century now, no one aboard and no weapons, a historical "
"relic, really. We need you to demolish it and bring us the stabilizers from "
"its jump drive which we can use to maintain our Hawking Scanners.\n"
"We have hacked the emergency integrity field so that the station can be "
"destroyed, but there were strange disturbances when we deactivated it. We're "
"not sure what it means, but we advise you to exercise caution...\n"
"%s"
msgstr "Great!\nThere is an old Exuari station, callsign X472, to the SE on the other side of the wormhole. It used to study the planet forming nearby, but it's been abandoned for over a century now, no one aboard and no weapons, a historical relic, really. We need you to demolish it and bring us the stabilizers from its jump drive which we can use to maintain our Hawking Scanners.\nWe have hacked the emergency integrity field so that the station can be destroyed, but there were strange disturbances when we deactivated it. We're not sure what it means, but we advise you to exercise caution...\n%s"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3697
msgctxt "KraylorWarning-incCall"
msgid ""
"Ugh, humans.\n"
"\n"
"This is the Kraylor Advanced \"Reasearch\" Project Agency (KARPA), we have "
"detected your suspicious activity in the vicinity.\n"
"\n"
"We are sending a team to investigate what you are up to. If you fire on us, "
"there will be trouble!"
msgstr "Ugh, humans.\n\nThis is the Kraylor Advanced \"Reasearch\" Project Agency (KARPA), we have detected your suspicious activity in the vicinity.\n\nWe are sending a team to investigate what you are up to. If you fire on us, there will be trouble!"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3707
msgctxt "KraylorWarning-shipLog"
msgid ""
"The Kraylor are investigating our activities and have warned us not to "
"escalate"
msgstr "The Kraylor are investigating our activities and have warned us not to escalate"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3724
msgctxt "wormhole-incCall"
msgid ""
"Great, you got the parts!\n"
"\n"
"You'd better hurry back, we've seen some Kraylor activity in the area. "
"Hopefully your salvage mission didn't attract the wrong sort of attention."
msgstr "Great, you got the parts!\n\nYou'd better hurry back, we've seen some Kraylor activity in the area. Hopefully your salvage mission didn't attract the wrong sort of attention."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3732
msgctxt "wormhole-shipLog"
msgid "Return the spare parts to the Wormhole Station"
msgstr "Return the spare parts to the Wormhole Station"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3748
msgctxt "wormhole-shipLog"
msgid "Jump Defence Activated"
msgstr "Jump Defence Activated"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3787
msgctxt "KraylorWarning-incCall"
msgid ""
"Watch your back, Hugh Mon!\n"
"\n"
"We don't know what you're up to, but we don't like the look of it. Keep your "
"distance and maybe we'll leave you alone.\n"
"\n"
"<The Kraylor Vessel jumps back through the wormhole>"
msgstr "Watch your back, Hugh Mon!\n\nWe don't know what you're up to, but we don't like the look of it. Keep your distance and maybe we'll leave you alone.\n\n<The Kraylor Vessel jumps back through the wormhole>"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3797
msgctxt "KraylorWarning-shipLog"
msgid "The Kraylor seem hostile and have warned us to keep our distance"
msgstr "The Kraylor seem hostile and have warned us to keep our distance"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3831
msgctxt "defenceStn-comms"
msgid "Good luck"
msgstr "Good luck"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3885
msgctxt "defenceStn-incCall"
msgid "Arrived, scan the security beacons"
msgstr "Arrived, scan the security beacons"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3895
msgctxt "defenceStn-incCall"
msgid ""
"Your cover has been blown and the proximity defense system remains active. "
"We suggest leaving and trying again to arrive with a future convoy."
msgstr "Your cover has been blown and the proximity defence system remains active. We suggest leaving and trying again to arrive with a future convoy."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3899
msgctxt "defenceStn-shipLog"
msgid "Our cover has been blown"
msgstr "Our cover has been blown"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3907
msgctxt "defenceStn-shipLog"
msgid "We should be good to try again"
msgstr "We should be good to try again"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3953
msgctxt "drone-incCall"
msgid ""
"Great work, Captain!\n"
"\n"
"We have taken control of this station and will be liquidating spare parts "
"from the wreckage."
msgstr "Great work, Captain!\n\nWe have taken control of this station and will be liquidating spare parts from the wreckage."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:3959
msgctxt "drone-shipLog"
msgid "DB-3 has a collection of spare parts"
msgstr "DB-3 has a collection of spare parts"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4051
msgctxt "wormhole-incCall"
msgid ""
"Thanks so much, captain!\n"
"\n"
"You really saved our ass there. Unfortunately our Hawking Scanner was "
"damaged by the bomb, and we haven't been able to get it back online. Do you "
"think you could get it fixed for us?\n"
"\n"
"Please dock with us to pick up the scanner."
msgstr "Thanks so much, captain!\n\nYou really saved our ass there. Unfortunately our Hawking Scanner was damaged by the bomb, and we haven't been able to get it back online. Do you think you could get it fixed for us?\n\nPlease dock with us to pick up the scanner."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4061
msgctxt "wormhole-shipLog"
msgid "Get the Hawking Scanner from the Wormhole Station"
msgstr "Get the Hawking Scanner from the Wormhole Station"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4129
msgctxt "drone-shipLog"
msgid ""
"This ship will not activate the drone station proximity defenses as long as "
"you arrive with a convoy."
msgstr "This ship will not activate the drone station proximity defences as long as you arrive with a convoy."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4137
msgctxt "drone-shipLog"
msgid "It's nice to be back aboard the Propitious 1"
msgstr "It's nice to be back aboard the Propitious 1"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4179
msgctxt "drone-incCall"
msgid "PROXIMITY DEFENCE SYSTEM ACTIVATED"
msgstr "PROXIMITY DEFENCE SYSTEM ACTIVATED"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4185
msgctxt "drone-shipLog"
msgid "We got too close to a drone station and it launched defenses."
msgstr "We got too close to a drone station and it launched defences."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4201
msgctxt "scienceDescription-beacons"
msgid ""
"The Ghosts drone security beacons. If we scan them all, we should be able to "
"find the control station. We'll need to get pretty close."
msgstr "The Ghosts drone security beacons. If we scan them all, we should be able to find the control station. We'll need to get pretty close."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4215
msgctxt "scienceDescription-beacons"
msgid ""
"The beamforming configuration from this beacon will help the boffins "
"triangulate the location of the central control."
msgstr "The beamforming configuration from this beacon will help the boffins triangulate the location of the central control."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4232
#, lua-format
msgctxt "defenceStn-incCall"
msgid ""
"Great work!\n"
"Our boffins were able to piece together the data and figure out where the "
"commands are coming from.\n"
"You must destroy station %s"
msgstr "Great work!\nOur boffins were able to piece together the data and figure out where the commands are coming from.\nYou must destroy station %s"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4241
#, lua-format
msgctxt "defenceStn-shipLog"
msgid "The drone control station is %s"
msgstr "The drone control station is %s"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4336
msgctxt "newShip-comms"
msgid "Too busy to talk today, Captain."
msgstr "Too busy to talk today, Captain."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4351
msgctxt "hendrixHints-comms"
msgid "Sorry, I don't know where Dr. Hendrix lives"
msgstr "Sorry, I don't know where Dr. Hendrix lives"

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4363
#, lua-format
msgctxt "hendrixHints-comms"
msgid ""
"Dr. Hendrix, of course! I'm pretty sure she was on a %s-class station, but "
"darned if I can remember which one."
msgstr "Dr. Hendrix, of course! I'm pretty sure she was on a %s-class station, but darned if I can remember which one."

#: scripts/scenario_30_broken_glass.lua:4371
#, lua-format
msgctxt "hendrixHints-comms"
msgid ""
"Gosh, Dr. Hendrix. Okay. Sorry, but honestly all I remember is that her "
"address definitely has a '%s' in it."
msgstr "Gosh, Dr. Hendrix. Okay. Sorry, but honestly all I remember is that her address definitely has a '%s' in it."

